<h1 class="h3 mb-3">About this project</h1>

<div class="row g-4">
    <div class="col-lg-8">
        <p>CEHR Health is a health-focused e-commerce platform developed for the <strong>CSC381 E-Commerce</strong> course (BSc CSIT, 6th semester). It is built with ASP.NET Core MVC, C#, Entity Framework Core and SQL Server.</p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">The case study vs. what we built</h2>
        <p>Our <em>case study</em> looks at Nepal's e-governance journey and a proposed <strong>Centralized Electronic Health Record (CEHR)</strong> — a national system that would connect a citizen's health information through a unique identity. Our <em>implementation</em> is the working online store you see here: a citizen (identified by a National ID) can browse medicines, medical equipment and health products, add them to a cart, check out, pay through a sandbox gateway, and track orders.</p>

        <div class="row g-3 my-2">
            <div class="col-md-6">
                <div class="card border-0 bg-light h-100">
                    <div class="card-body">
                        <div class="fw-semibold text-brand mb-1">Case study (context)</div>
                        <div class="small text-muted">Nepal E-Governance &rarr; CEHR &rarr; Citizen / NID</div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="col-md-6">
                <div class="card border-0 bg-light h-100">
                    <div class="card-body">
                        <div class="fw-semibold text-brand mb-1">This application (implementation)</div>
                        <div class="small text-muted">Citizen / NID &rarr; Health E-Commerce &rarr; Cart &rarr; Checkout &rarr; Payment &rarr; Orders</div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">National ID (NID)</h2>
        <p>Each citizen account carries a unique <strong>NID</strong>. It is the proposed identifier that a future CEHR could use to link a person to national health services. In this project the NID is a <strong>simulated, local identifier</strong> stored only in our own database.</p>

        <h2 class="h5 mt-4">Designed for the future, honest about today</h2>
        <p>The application is organised around clear service boundaries (products, cart, orders, payments, recommendations, citizen identity) so that a real CEHR/NID integration could be added later without rebuilding the store.</p>

        <div class="alert alert-warning mt-3">
            <i class="bi bi-exclamation-triangle"></i>
            <strong>Important:</strong> This is an academic prototype. It is <strong>not</strong> connected to any Government of Nepal NID or CEHR system, it does not process real prescriptions or real payments, and all products, prices and personal data are fictional/sample.
        </div>
    </div>

